openvino_bevfusion: cap the sparse encoder's OpenMP team, and let it run on a chosen GPU.

The sparse encoder builds CPU neighbour maps and scatters its output into
the dense BEV grid with OpenMP loops. Without OMP_NUM_THREADS, OpenMP starts
one thread per core, and these loops are short and memory bound: on a
128-thread two-socket Xeon the scatter took about 1.1 s per frame, against
about 0.1 s with four threads. Run both loops with at most four threads
unless OMP_NUM_THREADS is set.

The encoder also opened its OpenCL context on the first Intel GPU, so with
several GPUs it could run on a different one from the rest of the model.
BEVFUSION_OPENCL_DEVICE_UUID now picks the GPU by its UUID
(CL_DEVICE_UUID_KHR, the same 32 hex digits OpenVINO reports as a GPU's
DEVICE_UUID); unset keeps the first Intel GPU. It is read at the first
inference, as the context is process-wide.

Remove this patch once openvino_contrib carries an equivalent change.

